## Context
Line counts on origin/main: gaze 951, raid 509, roar 422, review-pr about 350, verify-adherence about 320. Each is read in full per run. `zotero`, `slides` and `route` already use `references/` to load detail on demand. In gaze the title says "six-phase", the description names four steps, and it calls `/review`, which is not a skill.

## Exit criteria
- [x] raid is split into a core plus `references/` files read at the phase that needs them: only branches a run uses sometimes move out (`rules/authoring-skills.md`: exclusivity, not length, is the test); measured 571 -> 444 lines in the core, seven references
- [x] Behaviour unchanged, shown by a byte comparison of core plus references against the old body (only intended edits differ) and the raid tests passing; gaze and roar were not touched here, so no dry run is owed
- [x] gaze title, description and phase list agree; the `/review` mention is a deliberate pointer to the native command, so it stays
- [x] gaze (951 -> 230 lines, tickets 1143/1144) and roar (422 -> 240 plus runbooks, ticket 1136) were shrunk by their own children; verify-gate (385) has no clean one-branch-of-many cut

## Children
- 1136 split roar (memory capture and pattern sweep out)
- 1140 demote step-only skills to scripts and runbooks
